1
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:09,300
Ta-da!

2
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:11,600
Wow...

3
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,867
It's so beautiful.

4
00:00:13,967 --> 00:00:17,333
Did you see that? It must've
jumped like 10 meters high.

5
00:00:18,267 --> 00:00:19,733
Woo-hoo!

6
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:36,233
Looks like we can go in here.

7
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:37,900
I think I'll go take a look.

8
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:43,467
Amazing.

9
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,200
How is it?

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,433
Your face is hilarious.

11
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:47,267
Huh?

12
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:48,633
So funny.

13
00:00:50,367 --> 00:00:52,233
I didn't even see any moray eels.

14
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:53,667
What about the moray eels?

15
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,409
Maybe they just don't like you.

16
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:57,513
You were definitely talking
trash about me just now.

17
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,300
No, I wasn't.

18
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:06,833
Here, Shiono, look this way.

19
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:08,700
- Okay.
- Give me a bigger smile.

20
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,000
I am smiling.

21
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,400
Not enough.

22
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,767
Smile a little more.

23
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:16,800
Say cheese.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,067
Not bad.

25
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:21,133
How many pictures are you going to take?

26
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,467
Wow, that's amazing.

27
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:32,700
Yeah.

28
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:52,400
Ah.

29
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:54,533
There's a turtle over there.

30
00:01:54,633 --> 00:01:55,867
Oh.

31
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:02,633
It's huge.

32
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,433
It really is.

33
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,776
I heard that one over
there is about 30 years old.

34
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:07,800
Yeah.

35
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,467
And this one here is around 50.

36
00:02:10,567 --> 00:02:12,133
Really?

37
00:02:20,033 --> 00:02:21,533
So cute.

38
00:02:22,133 --> 00:02:27,333
The Japanese name for spotted garden eels comes
from them looking like the Japanese Chin dog.

39
00:02:27,867 --> 00:02:31,667
Despite how they look,
they fight fiercely over territory.

40
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:33,967
Huh, really?

41
00:02:36,867 --> 00:02:38,400
Oh.

42
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,033
Jellyfish, jellyfish.

43
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:45,233
Jellyfish are over 95% water.

44
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:47,567
I heard they have no
brains and no emotions.

45
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:48,800
Huh?

46
00:02:49,667 --> 00:02:53,033
I'd love to just empty my mind
and drift around like that.

47
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:54,967
What are you talking about?

48
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,500
So cute.

49
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,600
Oh, aren't those penguins?

50
00:03:10,633 --> 00:03:13,567
I think penguins might be my favorite.

51
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,000
Penguins have complex
interpersonal relationships too.

52
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:20,000
No, wait, complex
"inter-penguin" relationships.

53
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,133
Complex inter-penguin relationships?

54
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:24,333
They actually cheat and
have affairs quite often.

55
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:26,009
Their relationships are pretty dramatic.

56
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:28,067
Huh, really?

57
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:30,067
Wow.

58
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,833
Shiono, you sure know a lot.

59
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:35,509
Do you really like aquariums?

60
00:03:35,533 --> 00:03:39,867
No, this is my first time
here since I grew up.

61
00:03:39,967 --> 00:03:42,600
But you know so much.

62
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:46,767
I looked it up beforehand.

63
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,300
Because I wanted Takoi-san
to have a good time.

64
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,567
Huh?

65
00:03:52,667 --> 00:03:55,000
I thought it'd be nice to
make some good memories.

66
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,467
After all, it's a date
with someone important.

67
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:01,133
A... a date?

68
00:04:01,633 --> 00:04:03,300
This is a date, right?

69
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:05,033
Isn't it?

70
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,300
A date...

71
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,000
This definitely counts as a date, right?

72
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,100
Yeah.

73
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:45,400
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

74
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:50,233
(Episode 5)

75
00:04:55,067 --> 00:04:55,900
Ah...

76
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,367
Hmm?

77
00:04:57,467 --> 00:04:59,033
These are limited-edition pens.

78
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:00,533
Oh, you're right.

79
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:02,333
I think I'll buy one too.

80
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,667
Should I get one for you as well?

81
00:05:09,233 --> 00:05:11,600
Ah, no need. You probably
don't need one either.

82
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:15,300
At our age, using matching
items is just too embarrassing.

83
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,033
Here.

84
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:26,767
This is for Takoi-san.

85
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,267
Thanks.

86
00:05:32,467 --> 00:05:35,967
It feels like we're a high school couple.

87
00:05:36,067 --> 00:05:38,533
That's hilarious.

88
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,267
When you asked me out,

89
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:53,733
I was actually relieved.

90
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:55,167
Huh?

91
00:05:55,467 --> 00:05:56,800
How should I put it...

92
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,800
I was actually really happy.

93
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:02,167
Hey, hurry up!

94
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:06,767
Ah.

95
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:32,900
Look, those two are holding hands.

96
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,567
Alright, stop staring, stop staring.

97
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,133
Ah.

98
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:43,867
Ah... there's a huge one here.

99
00:06:44,433 --> 00:06:45,733
Look.

100
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,400
You're right.

101
00:06:53,067 --> 00:06:54,533
See?

102
00:07:00,167 --> 00:07:01,900
Ah...

103
00:07:02,433 --> 00:07:04,267
It feels so therapeutic.

104
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:05,367
Really?

105
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:06,767
Yeah.

106
00:07:07,133 --> 00:07:08,933
That's good.

107
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,600
I want to come again.

108
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:18,133
Want to go grab a bite?

109
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:20,533
Hmm...

110
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:22,833
What's wrong?

111
00:07:22,933 --> 00:07:27,567
Nothing, I'm just a little
worried about Kamekichi.

112
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:30,667
Oh, I see.

113
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:37,600
So... if you don't mind,

114
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,733
Hmm?

115
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,633
Eat up.

116
00:07:47,367 --> 00:07:49,467
I went to see your friends today.

117
00:07:49,567 --> 00:07:51,333
Even saw a huge one.

118
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:19,100
Ah, please take care of that side too.

119
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,467
Okay.

120
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:30,267
Like this?

121
00:08:30,367 --> 00:08:31,400
Yeah.

122
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,333
Like this... no.

123
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:35,667
What is this?

124
00:08:35,767 --> 00:08:36,567
What?

125
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:38,300
No, I mean that shape.

126
00:08:39,233 --> 00:08:41,333
I'm not very good at this kind of stuff.

127
00:08:42,467 --> 00:08:43,667
Yeah, I figured.

128
00:08:44,367 --> 00:08:46,267
But once this stuff is cooked,

129
00:08:46,367 --> 00:08:48,033
doesn't it all taste the same?

130
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:52,967
You're just making excuses.

131
00:09:00,933 --> 00:09:02,867
Wait... wait a sec.

132
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:04,133
Damn it.

133
00:09:04,233 --> 00:09:05,667
Sigh...

134
00:09:06,433 --> 00:09:07,833
No.

135
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,567
Uh...

136
00:09:11,633 --> 00:09:15,000
I'd give it a 25 out of 100.

137
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:16,133
Huh?

138
00:09:16,233 --> 00:09:17,600
Isn't that a bit too harsh?

139
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,600
Eat it while it's hot.

140
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:20,900
Sure.

141
00:09:21,667 --> 00:09:23,033
Let's dig in.

142
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,700
Mmhmm.

143
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,333
It's good.

144
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,400
Let me ask you something.

145
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,260
Don't you get sick of
eating this every day?

146
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,800
Not at all.

147
00:09:40,033 --> 00:09:41,633
Let's dig in.

148
00:09:42,933 --> 00:09:44,167
Mmhmm.

149
00:09:44,267 --> 00:09:45,633
Delicious.

150
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:52,600
But eating it every day
must get boring, right?

151
00:09:57,467 --> 00:09:58,967
When you like something,

152
00:09:59,067 --> 00:10:01,427
you never get sick of it no
matter how much you eat, right?

153
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:03,367
Huh?

154
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:06,600
Even if you have it every day,

155
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,300
you won't get sick of it if you like it.

156
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:13,100
That's...

157
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,033
I see.

158
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,600
So that's how it is.

159
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,100
Yeah.

160
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,833
Mmhmm.

161
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,000
Mmhmm.

162
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:31,500
You've got some on your face.

163
00:10:32,367 --> 00:10:33,733
Sorry.

164
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,400
So cute.

165
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,667
Huh?

166
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:39,067
What's cute about it?

167
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,400
I'm a middle-aged man.

168
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,467
You being clumsy is cute too.

169
00:10:42,567 --> 00:10:44,200
I'm not clumsy.

170
00:10:44,767 --> 00:10:45,433
Are you blushing?

171
00:10:45,533 --> 00:10:47,033
I am not blushing.

172
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:49,100
- So cute.
- What's cute about it?!

173
00:10:49,433 --> 00:10:51,267
You're cute when you're mad too.

174
00:10:51,367 --> 00:10:52,933
Are you messing with me?

175
00:10:55,067 --> 00:10:56,833
Let me try cooking it again.

176
00:10:56,933 --> 00:10:58,443
It's all the same no matter what you use.

177
00:10:58,467 --> 00:11:00,233
I'll cook a perfect one for you to see.

178
00:11:01,167 --> 00:11:01,733
Really?

179
00:11:01,833 --> 00:11:03,167
Just you wait.

180
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:04,787
- No...
- Ah, you messed up right away.

181
00:11:04,867 --> 00:11:06,133
Wait a sec.

182
00:11:06,233 --> 00:11:08,700
No, it's over here.

183
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,276
And you haven't even
added the green onions yet.

184
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:11,767
Ah...

185
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:15,433
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

186
00:11:16,067 --> 00:11:18,900
Huh, transferred?

187
00:11:18,986 --> 00:11:22,453
Yeah, you're being transferred to
headquarters starting next month.

188
00:11:22,567 --> 00:11:24,067
Congratulations.

189
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:27,967
Got it.

190
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,000
Oh, Shiono.

191
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,467
Good work today.

192
00:11:39,567 --> 00:11:41,033
Good work.

193
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,100
What's up?

194
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,467
Oh, this?

195
00:11:44,567 --> 00:11:46,300
Shiraishi asked me to help organize.

196
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:48,433
And told me to clean up while I'm at it.

197
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:50,400
He sure knows how to boss people around.

198
00:11:54,633 --> 00:11:55,967
Hmm?

199
00:11:57,733 --> 00:12:01,867
Takoi-san, are you free tonight?

200
00:12:03,167 --> 00:12:05,433
Oh, of course I do.

201
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:07,567
I have something I want to tell you.

202
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:10,133
I see.

203
00:12:10,433 --> 00:12:12,067
Want to go to our usual spot?

204
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:14,409
It's Wednesday today.
There shouldn't be many regulars around.

205
00:12:14,433 --> 00:12:15,467
Okay.

206
00:12:15,933 --> 00:12:16,400
See you later then.

207
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:17,700
Yeah.

208
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:28,233
I was just here last week.

209
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:30,367
Why do I have to be the one doing this?

210
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,600
I've really had enough.

211
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,033
Need a hand?

212
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:47,733
Huh, what's up?

213
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:49,933
Since when are you so considerate?

214
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,000
Shiono.

215
00:12:53,567 --> 00:12:54,800
Yeah?

216
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:57,367
Help me with the top part too.

217
00:12:59,733 --> 00:13:01,133
Thanks.

218
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:04,400
I'll leave this to you from now on.

219
00:13:07,067 --> 00:13:08,567
Hey, Shiono.

220
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:13,333
Sure, if I'm still around.

221
00:13:14,433 --> 00:13:15,567
Huh?

222
00:13:29,233 --> 00:13:32,200
I'm heading to the
Criminal Affairs Division.

223
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,767
Okay.

224
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,733
Takoi-san.

225
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:44,200
Yeah?

226
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:46,000
This is so cute.

227
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,000
Huh?

228
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,833
Oh, this?

229
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:51,233
Don't tell me you two bought matching ones?

230
00:13:51,333 --> 00:13:52,500
Huh?

231
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,133
Matching ones.

232
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,800
What?

233
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:59,800
Did you two go on a trip together?

234
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,467
Yeah, you could say that.

235
00:14:02,567 --> 00:14:04,600
Nice, very nice.

236
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:06,433
So you bought matching ones?

237
00:14:06,533 --> 00:14:09,033
Wow, what matching things did you buy?

238
00:14:09,133 --> 00:14:09,967
Ah, it's nothing.

239
00:14:10,067 --> 00:14:11,067
So cute.

240
00:14:11,133 --> 00:14:13,243
Wait, did you get matching
ones with your girlfriend?

241
00:14:13,267 --> 00:14:14,300
No.

242
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,000
But it's really surprising.

243
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,733
Using matching items like this.

244
00:14:17,833 --> 00:14:19,700
It's so unlike Chief Takoi.

245
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,767
- Come on, Takoi-san.
- How rare.

246
00:14:21,867 --> 00:14:24,267
Sometimes I just feel
like using stuff like this.

247
00:14:24,367 --> 00:14:26,500
Don't get the wrong idea.

248
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,200
Someone gave it to me,
so I just started using it.

249
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:30,433
Really?

250
00:14:30,533 --> 00:14:31,133
- I'm telling you.
- Highly suspicious.

251
00:14:31,233 --> 00:14:32,609
- You're not a student.
- Your face says it all.

252
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:35,133
Who uses matching stuff at your age?

253
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:36,667
- Takoi-san.
- Is that so?

254
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:43,200
Here's the certificate you asked for.

255
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:45,033
Please get this signed for me.

256
00:14:46,867 --> 00:14:47,900
Okay.

257
00:14:50,333 --> 00:14:51,833
I'll be going now.

258
00:14:55,467 --> 00:14:58,100
Alright, back to work.

259
00:15:05,133 --> 00:15:06,600
Something on your mind?

260
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,067
Huh?

261
00:15:08,233 --> 00:15:10,133
Thinking about Shiono?

262
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:11,167
What?

263
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:13,867
You two seem pretty close.

264
00:15:20,467 --> 00:15:21,833
It's fine.

265
00:15:22,167 --> 00:15:23,767
I haven't told anyone.

266
00:15:26,367 --> 00:15:27,767
Heh.

267
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:32,533
You finally found a good catch.

268
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:36,333
What are you talking about?

269
00:15:36,433 --> 00:15:37,933
That guy is a total handful.

270
00:15:38,033 --> 00:15:39,367
What are you saying?

271
00:15:39,467 --> 00:15:40,933
You're not much different yourself.

272
00:15:41,033 --> 00:15:42,333
True that.

273
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,167
Congratulations.

274
00:15:48,133 --> 00:15:49,367
Oh.

275
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:31,300
Huh? So you do have a cute side.

276
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,433
Cute, my foot.

277
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,567
It's just a huge hassle.

278
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,733
Showing off your romance.

279
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,400
Oh, welcome.

280
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,267
It's so hot!

281
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:42,433
Huh?

282
00:16:43,233 --> 00:16:45,776
Strange, don't you guys usually
go somewhere else on Wednesdays?

283
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:49,067
Oh, heard they're closed today.

284
00:16:49,167 --> 00:16:50,533
We had no choice but to come here.

285
00:16:50,633 --> 00:16:52,600
What do you mean, "no choice"?

286
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:53,700
Ah, two draft beers.

287
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,867
Coming right up.

288
00:16:54,967 --> 00:16:56,867
Oh man.

289
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,833
Ah, right, Takoi.

290
00:16:59,133 --> 00:17:01,433
I heard you used that ticket.

291
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:02,700
Huh?

292
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,533
I heard.

293
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:08,000
You were at the aquarium with a guy.

294
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:09,867
My friend saw you.

295
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:12,033
I thought you'd ask a girl out.

296
00:17:12,133 --> 00:17:14,400
Don't tell me you've
finally switched to guys?

297
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,400
Wait, seriously?

298
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,800
Hey, Takoi.

299
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,400
Did you come out of the closet?

300
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:21,600
- Oh, for real?
- Did you get a boyfriend?

301
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:23,067
Maybe he really is into guys now.

302
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,209
- Then just give it a try.
- No way, that's too hard to swallow.

303
00:17:25,233 --> 00:17:27,733
- Yeah, that's a bit too intense.
- This is huge.

304
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:29,700
- Guys are fine too.
- You caught me?

305
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,800
Huh?

306
00:17:32,233 --> 00:17:35,733
Actually, I can swing that way too.

307
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:37,600
Just kidding.

308
00:17:37,786 --> 00:17:39,419
- What the hell?
- What was that about?

309
00:17:39,533 --> 00:17:41,533
You totally had us fooled.

310
00:17:45,267 --> 00:17:46,633
As if that's possible.

311
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:47,733
What if I really was?

312
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,433
What would you do?

313
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:50,067
No, no way.

314
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:51,367
I'm kidding, just kidding.

315
00:17:51,467 --> 00:17:52,167
Takoi.

316
00:17:52,267 --> 00:17:53,767
I just saw Shiono looking lonely.

317
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:56,267
So I asked him out.

318
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:59,133
How could I ever date a guy?

319
00:17:59,233 --> 00:18:02,333
Don't think of me as some creep.

320
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:05,400
Then hurry up and get a girlfriend.

321
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:06,833
I know, I know.

322
00:18:06,933 --> 00:18:08,767
That's why I'm telling you to find a woman.

323
00:18:09,567 --> 00:18:10,667
Takoi-san.

324
00:18:10,767 --> 00:18:12,309
- Stop messing with me.
- You're the one who bluffed us.

325
00:18:12,333 --> 00:18:17,333
- No, listen to me.
- You have to take responsibility.

326
00:18:19,733 --> 00:18:21,100
Thanks.

327
00:18:23,933 --> 00:18:25,233
What?

328
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,400
Whether it's to yourself.

329
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,167
Or to others.

330
00:18:30,267 --> 00:18:32,800
Don't say such degrading things.

331
00:18:44,467 --> 00:18:46,933
What's up with Shiono?

332
00:18:48,167 --> 00:18:51,100
He's not returning my calls.

333
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:12,400
What are you doing?

334
00:19:14,033 --> 00:19:15,733
If someone sees you in a place like this.

335
00:19:19,433 --> 00:19:21,113
You won't be able to drink anymore, right?

336
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:26,033
Alright.

337
00:19:26,133 --> 00:19:28,009
- Anyway, let's head back first.
- I'm giving up.

338
00:19:28,033 --> 00:19:29,200
Huh?

339
00:19:31,133 --> 00:19:32,413
I don't want to do this anymore.

340
00:19:39,933 --> 00:19:41,467
About us kissing.

341
00:19:42,167 --> 00:19:43,833
And me saying I like you.

342
00:19:44,367 --> 00:19:45,933
Please forget all of it.

343
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,833
I'm being transferred.

344
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,333
What?

345
00:19:53,967 --> 00:19:55,767
I'm transferring to headquarters.

346
00:19:57,567 --> 00:19:59,167
So isn't this perfect?

347
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,400
What do you mean, "perfect"?

348
00:20:03,067 --> 00:20:05,643
Even if you transfer, it's not like
we'll be too far to see each other.

349
00:20:05,667 --> 00:20:08,147
- Why the sudden change?
- You think I'm disgusting, don't you?

350
00:20:08,333 --> 00:20:09,833
Don't you?

351
00:20:12,433 --> 00:20:15,100
"How could I ever date a guy?"

352
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:18,867
"I just saw him looking lonely,
so I asked him out."

353
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,033
"Don't think of me as some creep."

354
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:28,733
Whatever others say.

355
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:31,200
Or how they see me, I don't care.

356
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,967
It has absolutely nothing to do with me.

357
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
But.

358
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,667
If even Takoi-san says things like that.

359
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:42,233
It really hurts.

360
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:49,600
No, about that.

361
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:51,967
I'm sorry.

362
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:55,167
But that was the only
thing I could say at the time.

363
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:59,000
I was afraid that talking about it in that
situation would make you uncomfortable.

364
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:03,033
And ruin the mood.

365
00:21:04,933 --> 00:21:06,267
I'm really sorry, um.

366
00:21:06,367 --> 00:21:08,233
This isn't about apologizing.

367
00:21:12,033 --> 00:21:13,500
At the end of the day.

368
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,733
I'm just not the one you want.

369
00:21:18,933 --> 00:21:20,600
To you.

370
00:21:21,667 --> 00:21:23,800
I'm ultimately not the right person.

371
00:21:28,033 --> 00:21:30,500
I'm sorry for forcing you to
go along with me until now.

372
00:21:38,733 --> 00:21:40,133
I've been really happy lately.

373
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:45,700
Goodbye, Takoi-san.

374
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:13,767
(Next Episode)
Can you do it?

375
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,600
Can you kiss me right here?

376
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,900
Shiono is getting transferred.

377
00:22:17,967 --> 00:22:19,976
Once he leaves, it'll be hard
for you two to see each other.

378
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,500
Go find someone you can proudly show off.

379
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:23,900
And have a normal relationship.

380
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,667
I think that suits you better.

381
00:22:25,767 --> 00:22:27,000
Chief Takoi.

382
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:28,100
Shiono!

383
00:22:28,133 --> 00:22:31,533
That guy Shiono is definitely
going to climb the ranks.

384
00:22:31,633 --> 00:22:33,067
Hey, you're way too tense.

385
00:22:33,167 --> 00:22:34,400
Loosen up a bit.
